
 fillcodusage - Fill table 'codusage' from custom OPeNDAP (COD) access logs.

 Reads RDA Web/COD access logs under /var/log and inserts usage records
 into the 'codusage' table in PostgreSQL database 'rdadb'.

 USAGE:
   fillcodusage [-b] (-a | -d LogEntryDates | -f LogFileNames | -m MonthList |
                      -N NumberDays | -p BeginDate [EndDate] | -y YearList)

 OPTIONS (choose exactly one of -a, -d, -f, -m, -N, -p, or -y):

   -a   Process all available log files.

   -d LogEntryDates
        Process the given dates. Date format: YYYY-MM-DD (e.g. 2024-01-15).
        A log file holds a whole month, so the months holding these dates are
        read and only entries falling on the given dates are recorded.

   -f LogFileNames
        Process the given log file names directly.

   -m MonthList
        Process log files for the given months.
        Month format: YYYY-MM (e.g. 2024-01).

   -N NumberDays
        Process log files covering the most recent NumberDays days.

   -p BeginDate [EndDate]
        Process log entries between BeginDate and EndDate, inclusive.
        EndDate defaults to today if omitted. As with -d, whole months are
        read and the entries outside the range are skipped.

   -y YearList
        Process log files for the given years.
        Year format: YYYY (e.g. 2024).

   -b   Run in background mode (log to file only, no terminal output).

 EXAMPLE:
   fillcodusage -m 2024-01 2024-02
   fillcodusage -d 2024-01-15 2024-02-03
